I think that the problem was an omission of the order of the variable labels.  When I run

dd<-data.frame(sex=factor(c(rep("Women",3), rep("Men",7)),ordered=TRUE, levels=c("Women","Men")),ind=c(paste("Women", 1:3), paste("Men", 1:7)), val=1:10)
ddply(dd, .(sex), numcolwise(mean))

I get

> dd<-data.frame(sex=factor(c(rep("Women",3), rep("Men",7)),ordered=TRUE, levels=c("Women","Men")),ind=c(paste("Women", 1:3), paste("Men", 1:7)), val=1:10)
> ddply(dd, .(sex), numcolwise(mean))
    sex val
1 Women   2
2   Men   7

Which lists in level order.

-Andrew

