Dear Fellow Data Rangers,

I used the R package "oligo"  to translate microarray image files (.CEL) into a normalized expression dataset. The best, and most intense, method yields a comma separated table topping 110MB that is laid out the wrong way. I need to transpose it. Excel and Origin fail. I tried the simple R script below. It takes HOURS to read in the table, then R crashes after entering the transpose line (PC and Mac, 64bit and old school on well-equipped desktops). I've opened the file within a text editor and it reads fine. I am going to next try it on a Linux system, perhaps that won't crash...

Thank you very much for your suggestions & ignorance tolerance.

#Begin
#Read in the csv file created by oligo
oligo<-read.table(file.choose())
#transpose
t(oligo)
#End

