Justin (and Andrew),

You are both correct. The example I created was not something suitable
for parallel processing because the overhead cost more time than the
speedup. With your example the timing advantage is more clear. In
fact, each parallel part was so fleeting that I could not see the
spawned R processes appear in the top output.

Thanks!

Eric

